.\" Man page for TCM — Terminal Connection Manager
.\" Generated for TCM version 1.0.0
.TH TCM 1 "May 2026" "TCM 1.0.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
tcm \- Terminal Connection Manager — TUI multiplexer for SSH, Telnet, and Serial sessions

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tcm
[\fIOPTION\fR]...

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tcm
is a terminal-based connection manager for network engineers and system administrators.
It provides a unified TUI interface to manage multiple concurrent SSH, Telnet, and
Serial (RS-232) connections, with support for macro automation via JSON recipe files,
session logging in Asciicast v2 format, and encrypted credential storage.

Sessions are persisted across restarts in
.IR ~/.config/tcm/sessions.json .
The session list is displayed on launch; use the keyboard shortcuts below to navigate,
connect, and manage sessions.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version string and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-config \fIPATH\fR
Load sessions from \fIPATH\fR instead of the default
.IR ~/.config/tcm/sessions.json .
.TP
.B \-\-log\-dir \fIDIR\fR
Write Asciicast log files to \fIDIR\fR instead of the default
.IR ~/.local/share/tcm/logs/ .

.SH KEY BINDINGS

.SS Session List
.TP
.BR j ", " \[da]
Move selection down.
.TP
.BR k ", " \[ua]
Move selection up.
.TP
.BR Enter ", " c
Connect to the selected session.
.TP
.B n
Open the New Session form.
.TP
.B e
Edit the selected session.
.TP
.B d
Delete the selected session (with confirmation).
.TP
.B m
Open the recipe picker and run a macro against the selected session.
.TP
.B q
Quit TCM.

.SS Connected Session (prefix: Ctrl-b)
.TP
.B Ctrl-b
Open the session switcher overlay.
.TP
.B Ctrl-b d
Detach from the current session and return to the session list.
.TP
.B Ctrl-b n
Switch to the next session.
.TP
.B Ctrl-b p
Switch to the previous session.
.TP
.B Ctrl-b q
Quit TCM.

.SS Switcher Overlay
.TP
.BR j ", " \[da]
Move selection down.
.TP
.BR k ", " \[ua]
Move selection up.
.TP
.B Enter
Switch to the selected session.
.TP
.BR Esc ", " q
Close the overlay without switching.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/tcm/sessions.json
Session database. Contains an array of session objects in JSON format.
.TP
.I ~/.config/tcm/recipes/
Directory for recipe (macro) JSON files. See
.BR tcm-recipe (5)
or
.I docs/recipe-format.md
for the recipe format specification.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/tcm/logs/
Asciicast v2 session logs. Each log is named
.IR <session-name>-<timestamp>.cast .

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Launch TCM:
.B tcm

.TP
Launch with a custom session file:
.B tcm --config /etc/tcm/lab-sessions.json

.TP
Launch with logs written to a custom directory:
.B tcm --log-dir /var/log/tcm

.SH SESSION JSON FORMAT
A session object in
.I sessions.json
has the following shape (protocol-specific fields vary):

.EX
  {
    "name":        "prod-router",
    "protocol":    "ssh",
    "host":        "10.0.0.1",
    "port":        22,
    "username":    "admin",
    "auth_method": "password"
  }
.EE

Supported values for
.B protocol
are
.BR ssh ,
.BR telnet ,
and
.BR serial .

For serial sessions, use
.BR device ,
.BR baud_rate ,
.BR data_bits ,
.BR parity ,
and
.B stop_bits
instead of
.B host
and
.BR port .

.SH BUILDING FROM SOURCE
.EX
  git clone <repo-url>
  cd tcm
  ./scripts/build.sh --release
  ./scripts/install.sh
.EE

Pass
.B --asan
to enable AddressSanitizer during development.
Pass
.B --static
to link
.I libgcc
and
.I libstdc++
statically into the binary.

